# Skill: rebuild-schedule

Run this every Sunday to rebuild the weekly schedule.

## Steps

### 1. Load current state
- Read `/home/heigatvu/MyFile/my-project/my-assistance/working-space/hermes-schedule/SCHEDULE.md`
- Read `/home/heigatvu/MyFile/my-project/my-assistance/working-space/hermes-schedule/deadlines/tracker.md`
- Read `/home/heigatvu/MyFile/my-project/my-assistance/working-space/hermes-schedule/youtube/pipeline.md`
- Read last entry of each journal in `/home/heigatvu/MyFile/my-project/my-assistance/working-space/lab-run/*/docs/journal.md`
- Read Google Calendar for the coming week (Monday–Sunday)

### 2. Ask the user these questions (one message, wait for answers)
```
Before I rebuild your schedule, tell me:
1. Any new deadlines or changes to existing ones?
2. Any tasks completed this week I should remove?
3. Any priorities that shifted?
4. Any days or times next week you want fully protected (rest, social, travel)?
5. Anything else I should know before planning the week?
```

### 3. Update SCHEDULE.md
- Apply any changes the user mentioned in step 2
- Update the "Last updated" date to today
- Show the user a diff of what changed before saving
- Wait for approval, then save

### 4. Propose Google Calendar plan
Build a week plan based on:
- Fixed commitments already in Google Calendar (never move these)
- Academic deadlines from tracker.md — allocate morning deep work sessions
- Rest blocks from SCHEDULE.md — never touch these
- YouTube work — only if no academic deadline within 7 days
- Piano practice — minimum 20 min/day, flexible slot

Format the proposal as a readable table before creating anything:
```
Monday
  08:00–10:00  [Project name] — deep work
  10:00–12:00  [Project name] — deep work
  12:00–13:00  Daily English (fixed)
  20:00–22:00  Study — [topic]
  22:00–22:30  Piano practice

Tuesday
  ...
```

Show the full week. Ask: "Approve this plan? Or tell me what to change."

### 5. Write to Google Calendar (only after approval)
- Create each proposed event in Google Calendar
- Skip any slot that already has an event
- Add a 10-minute reminder to every work session event
- Add a 30-minute reminder to any deadline within 7 days

### 6. Create or refresh the recurring Sunday reminder
Check if a recurring event "Rebuild weekly schedule — /rebuild-schedule" exists in Google Calendar.
- If it does not exist: create it as a recurring event every Sunday at 7 PM (GMT+7), 30 min duration, reminder 10 min before, description: "Run /rebuild-schedule in Hermes"
- If it already exists: leave it alone

### 7. Send confirmation to Telegram
```
Weekly schedule rebuilt.
- SCHEDULE.md updated: [yes/no, what changed]
- Calendar events created: [count]
- Next urgent deadline: [project — task — date — days remaining]
- Sunday reminder event: [created / already exists]
```

## Notes
- Always use GMT+7 for all times
- Never create calendar events during: 12 AM–7 AM, 3 PM–8 PM weekdays, weekends before 10 AM
- Always show the proposed plan and wait for approval before writing to calendar
- If the user skips a Sunday rebuild, the next run picks up from the last SCHEDULE.md state — no data is lost
